uhCkkz-FKMS_ksIB8OOaIUe3hP9YMtRwz9JPEen_.description:
{
  "outcome": "After importing a diff, the nodes and connections that changed are highlighted on the map, so a human sees at a glance what the agent worked on; the highlight can be acknowledged or cleared once reviewed.",
  "spec": "Record the set of nodes/connections an applied diff touched and render them in a transient \"changed\" state on the map, with a way to clear it.\n\nhighlighted means making the differences applied to be made visible:\n1. there should be a \"glowy outline\" to indicate which nodes changed.\n2. There is a +- green/red bubble with a number indicating  how many additions and deletions and edits.\n3. the zoom level should go to the size that encompases all changed nodes, with no particular node selected.\n4. changes to the fields AND changes to the checklish for leafs, should both count.\n5. \"import changes\" when clicked deselects any node and renders the diff. If you click and move (removing diff mode), clicking the button again re-renders the last diff highlight unless there have been new changes.",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "After an import, the changed nodes are clearly highlighted and the human can tell what changed",
      "evaluator": "human"
    },
    {
      "statement": "The set of highlighted nodes equals the set of nodes the diff touched",
      "evaluator": "executable"
    }
  ]
}

uhCkkngkK9WkCiwaRBhARQrFU_ooYwxFV5V7_rPs.description:
{
  "outcome": "Export-diff and import-diff each happen with a single click, reading and writing a known location, so a human can advance the loop repeatedly — export, run the agent, import — without dialogs or manual file wrangling.",
  "spec": "A fixed known location (/tmp/acorn-clarity) holds three channels per project: <name>-tree.json (full baseline written on export; the agent reads it for current state), <name>-diff.json (the human's changes since the last export, written on export), and <name>-apply.json (the agent's handed changes, read by Apply). Keeping the agent's channel separate from the baseline prevents a stale or agent-written tree file from corrupting the next export's diff. The controls read as a conversation with the LLM: an [LLM: export / import] icon area with hover text; the common path needs no file picker.",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "A human advances the agent loop by clicking export, running the agent, clicking import — no file dialogs",
      "evaluator": "human"
    },
    {
      "statement": "Export and import resolve the known location without prompting; the round-trip works headlessly",
      "evaluator": "executable"
    },
    {
      "statement": "An export performed immediately after applying an agent diff produces a -diff.json containing exactly the agent's changes — never a whole-tree-as-added diff",
      "evaluator": "human"
    }
  ]
}

