  "outcome": "An agent that finishes work on a node posts its results back onto that node — a completion verdict {pass/fail, evidence} and any produced artifacts — through the same propose_edits write-back the MCP surface already provides, and the node's status reflects a passing executable criterion. This is the 'results return' arrow of the work loop; it pairs with the human-confirm path (loop-eval-signal) as the agent-confirm path. The agent is the fly on the wall.",
