uhCkkElJz1q0VLwHZPmW-_RzRgm8kwD3PTIbF8OE.description:
{
  "outcome": "Between last export to llm a human may have made changes.  Importing an LLM's changes should not override them.  If there are merge conflicts this should be flagged.   i.e. it should not just be importing a whole tree, it should be integrating the specific changes of the diff.",
  "spec": "Apply performs a three-way merge: the agent's diff is compared against both the live tree and the last-export baseline (the snapshot saved when the human exported). For each node the agent updates — if the human also changed it since the export (live differs from baseline) and the agent's value differs from the live value, that node is a conflict: flagged for review, never silently overwritten. Non-conflicting agent changes apply normally.",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "A node edited by the human after export and also updated by the agent's diff is flagged as a conflict, and the human's live value is not silently overwritten",
      "evaluator": "human"
    },
    {
      "statement": "Merge logic is pure and unit-tested: agent-only change applies; human-only change persists; both-changed flags a conflict",
      "evaluator": "executable"
    }
  ]
}

