uhCkksSbsbihT6XByEgadP9svUFaANFjZPwPmwW6.description:
{
  "outcome": "Humans run the full lifecycle of a leaf — see what's ready to build, start the work, watch it move to 'awaiting evaluation', and confirm completion — as one low-friction flow, with each leaf's place in that lifecycle legible at a glance on the map. You never have to guess what state a leaf is in or what it needs from you next.",
  "handle": "work-loop",
  "spec": "A flow view of the leaf lifecycle belongs here (a diagram, not a list): ready-to-build → in-progress → awaiting-human-evaluation → achieved, with the transitions a human or agent drives. The phase capabilities live on the children — readiness signals when to start, the trigger starts the work, completion evaluates and records done-ness; this branch's own job is to make the whole loop legible and the 'this needs you' moments obvious.",
  "principle": "The human is the evaluator of last resort: a leaf waiting on a human decision must be visually unmistakable, and confirming it must be a single click."
}

